cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "Polymorphic Decision Protocol"
abstract: >-
  A procedure for making high-uncertainty decisions with panels of AI systems,
  where consensus is discounted by input provenance, model confidence is tested
  under controlled pressure, and the human owns the weights, the stakes, and the
  exit.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shallbetter
    given-names: Zachary
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9450-3429"
version: "1.4.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zachshallbetter/polymorphic-decision-protocol"
url: "https://polymorphic-decision-protocol.vercel.app"
keywords:
  - decision protocol
  - high-uncertainty decisions
  - provenance
  - calibration
  - human-in-the-loop
  - panel methods
abstract: >-
  PDP Local Toolkit provides a local, human-gated workflow for the Polymorphic
  Decision Protocol normative candidate, including encrypted records, approved
  model calls, search, stress testing, commitment review, monitoring, settlement,
  and audit. It does not execute consequential actions or establish empirical
  validity.
identifiers:
